title: Cursor - evolution of multi-agent coordination
---
%%{init: {"theme":"base","themeVariables":{"fontFamily":"Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif","fontSize":"14px","lineColor":"#555555","background":"#ffffff"}}}%%
flowchart TD
  A["1. Flat agents + shared file with locks"]:::code
  AP["Stalls, never-released locks:<br/>20 agents performed like 2 or 3"]:::risk
  B["2. Optimistic concurrency"]:::code
  BP["Sturdier, but agents became<br/>risk-averse and avoided hard tasks"]:::risk
  subgraph C ["3. Planners / workers / judge"]
    direction TB
    PL["Planners explore and spawn<br/>tasks (recursively)"]:::llm
    WK["Workers do one task,<br/>ignore coordination"]:::llm
    JG["Judge decides whether to continue"]:::llm
    PL -->|tasks| WK
    WK -->|results| JG
    JG -->|continue: fresh restart<br/>each cycle| PL
  end
  D["Later: integrator QC role added"]:::code
  DP["Became a bottleneck"]:::risk
  E["Integrator removed"]:::code
  R["Outcome: hundreds of concurrent agents,<br/>browser from scratch in ~1 week (1M+ LoC)"]:::ext

  A --> AP
  AP -->|replaced by| B
  B --> BP
  BP -->|replaced by| C
  C --> D
  D --> DP
  DP -->|deleted| E
  E --> R
